+// 2026-09-21: ILA instance removed.
+//
+// haps_top.sv and haps_top.xdc have both stated since 2026-08-11 that the ILA
+// was removed and debug_uart_probe is the sole debug channel, because JTAG
+// readback is confirmed corrupt at 20 MHz on this board (Xicom 50-38/50-41,
+// frozen clock-toggle probe, simultaneous glitches on unrelated signals). But
+// this instance was still live: FPGA_BUILD *is* defined for synthesis
+// (set_property verilog_define FPGA_BUILD), so every build carried the ILA,
+// the debug hub and its BSCAN/JTAG clock domain - confirmed on the routed
+// netlist of 2026-09-21, where dbg_hub's INTERNAL_TCK appears as one of only
+// two constrained clocks in the design.
+//
+// Removing it drops that clock domain, the hub, and the ila_1 OOC synthesis
+// run. If ILA visibility is ever wanted again, re-instantiate at the top level
+// alongside the other debug taps rather than inside a reusable leaf module,
+// and drop the design clock first so readback is trustworthy.
+//
+// ila_1 u_rom_ila (
+//     .clk    (ACLK),
+//     .probe0 (ARVALID),          // 1   CPU issuing a fetch?
+//     .probe1 (ARADDR),           // 32  ...to what byte address (expect 0x0, +8)
+//     .probe2 (ARREADY),          // 1
+//     .probe3 (RVALID),           // 1   read response returning?
+//     .probe4 (RREADY),           // 1
+//     .probe5 (RRESP),            // 2   00=OKAY, 11=DECERR
